    "narrative": "With the 2026 season reaching this critical juncture, our priority remains the pursuit of stolen bases and efficient contact. **Brice Turang** earns the nod today with a 46.51 score, a play driven almost entirely by his aggressive baserunning profile against a pitcher in Skubal who, despite an elite 2.85 xERA, is susceptible to the running game. While the matchup against such a high-tier arm typically warrants caution, **Brice Turang**\u2019s placement in the #2 hole and his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s deliberate delivery keep his floor high enough for an active start. We are essentially betting on **Brice Turang** to manufacture value through disruption rather than raw slugging.\n\nOur bench remains heavily populated by inactivity today, as **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** are all sidelined by team off-days, and **Tyler Soderstrom** continues to navigate his IL stint. Consequently, there were no difficult \"trimming\" decisions required at the margins this morning; the lack of available volume has forced our hand. Looking ahead, we need to monitor the health of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Jose Caballero**, as their availability will be pivotal for maintaining our SB pace in the coming week. With **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** also off the field today, the Ghost Ride the WHIP roster is effectively in a holding pattern. Exercise caution; we are playing for game-cap preservation until the schedule deepens tomorrow.",
